                    {
                        "form_id": "5bc9944b-3afa-4815-a8b9-3f579667078e",
                        "entry_id": "5bf2b111-9b0d-3c71-a2b0-9fc7e012e594",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "prepositional"
                        ],
                        "form": "злоключе́ниях"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "8e8a438b-5731-3dd5-9ffd-cd91e7f04866",
                        "entry_id": "5bf2b111-9b0d-3c71-a2b0-9fc7e012e594",
                        "glosses": [
                            "несчастное приключение; бедствие, несчастье"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "7fcb2661-9d43-4b84-8274-e3f088379445",
                                "sense_id": "8e8a438b-5731-3dd5-9ffd-cd91e7f04866",
                                "text": "Описывать свои злоключения в ремстройконторе не буду, они знакомы каждому. Сначала затерялся наряд, потом выяснилось, что клеевую окраску делает только один маляр, а его нет, он сейчас работает где-то на улице Горького, и, сколько ещё там провозится, неизвестно ― может, неделю, а может, месяц."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3aa43604-2d1b-4225-bf18-e0ffaad8a2b9",
                                "sense_id": "8e8a438b-5731-3dd5-9ffd-cd91e7f04866",
                                "text": "Я рассказал ему о своих злоключениях — как мне пытались пришить уголовное дело, как на меня давят…"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "4a9da8f5-8952-4be2-bc68-c3b912b4a17e",
                        "source_entry_id": "5bf2b111-9b0d-3c71-a2b0-9fc7e012e594",
                        "source_sense_id": "8e8a438b-5731-3dd5-9ffd-cd91e7f04866",
                        "target_lang_word": "mishap",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "mishap",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5ee3e24d-b410-393b-9e2c-ab9325a27d0b",
                                        "entry_id": "e42ff749-31f8-3531-a2c6-5e62dc3ab9ad",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An accident, mistake, or problem."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "49b16b8d-c155-4a10-b1b2-98d84ec8acf3",
                                                "sense_id": "5ee3e24d-b410-393b-9e2c-ab9325a27d0b",
                                                "text": "Since the mishap with the banana peel, he watches his step."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9cc3756f-61c3-45a2-97c8-63fa3fa5a811",
                                                "sense_id": "5ee3e24d-b410-393b-9e2c-ab9325a27d0b",
                                                "text": "He had come straight up without mishap or swerving off his course, and his shut teeth unlocked."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d912f9d3-e724-499a-9073-68389f9d17da",
                                                "sense_id": "5ee3e24d-b410-393b-9e2c-ab9325a27d0b",
                                                "text": "“Israel deeply regrets the tragic mishap that occurred today at the Nasser Hospital,” the office said in a statement. It went on to say that “Israel values the work of journalists, medical staff and all civilians.”"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "357ef063-a097-3935-9346-4926295f8999",
                                        "entry_id": "e42ff749-31f8-3531-a2c6-5e62dc3ab9ad",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Ill luck; misfortune; mischance."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e0dd2377-b467-4eda-add6-0d82ca657a16",
                                                "sense_id": "357ef063-a097-3935-9346-4926295f8999",
                                                "text": "Rome’s readiest champions, repose you here in rest,\nSecure from worldly chances and mishaps!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c8ca0852-5d33-4f44-b793-f46336b84181",
                                                "sense_id": "357ef063-a097-3935-9346-4926295f8999",
                                                "text": "He ſvvet and ſvvet againe vvith ſuch exceſſiue ſvvoonings, as not only himſelfe, but likevviſe all the beholders, did verily deeme, that his life vvas ending. This ſtorme and miſhappe endured about ſome tvvo hovvres, after vvhich hee remayned not cured as his Maſter, but ſo vveary and indiſpoſed, as hee vvas not able to ſtand."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "12264875-2f89-48cf-b621-b9c6a9526afe",
                                                "sense_id": "357ef063-a097-3935-9346-4926295f8999",
                                                "text": "There are certain ceremonies which are observed once a year by a whole community or village, and are intended to safeguard its members from dangers of the forest, and from sickness and mishap during the coming twelve months."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "mishap",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "94c59b05-876e-3a7f-b995-f8f220f420c1",
                                        "entry_id": "7e0867e1-9789-3380-a4c1-579882564f1a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To happen through misfortune; to mishappen."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic",
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "e0b6d5f9-b8ab-4db8-955f-15af4598fb4e",
                        "source_entry_id": "5bf2b111-9b0d-3c71-a2b0-9fc7e012e594",
                        "source_sense_id": "8e8a438b-5731-3dd5-9ffd-cd91e7f04866",
                        "target_lang_word": "misadventure",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "misadventure",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ed8302ff-fb00-341a-8f0d-063d9b6498b2",
                                        "entry_id": "d90737c4-62fa-3660-9961-3474abe14615",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An accidental mishap or misfortune."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9e05bc88-db99-4e92-910f-df717adeca6a",
                                                "sense_id": "ed8302ff-fb00-341a-8f0d-063d9b6498b2",
                                                "text": "It is said that every life has its roses and thorns; there seemed, however, to have been a misadventure or mistake in Stephen's case, whereby somebody else had become possessed of his roses, and he had become possessed of the same somebody else's thorns in addition to his own."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "36b378af-535b-410d-954a-8f76b8766e9e",
                                                "sense_id": "ed8302ff-fb00-341a-8f0d-063d9b6498b2",
                                                "text": "There were, however, 34 deaths among passengers in movement accidents, due mainly to misadventure and carelessness when entering and leaving trains in motion, falling off platforms and out of carriages, and opening and closing carriage doors."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
